# Admin

`/admin` sits outside the wallet layout. `openAdmin()` in `lib/admin.server.ts` reads the Better Auth session and allows the visit only when that Google email is in the `ADMIN_EMAILS` env var (comma-separated). Comparison ignores case and surrounding spaces. Read it as `process.env.ADMIN_EMAILS`. An empty value lets nobody in. A signed-out visit shows the sign-in screen and returns to `/admin`. A signed-in account that is not on the list gets the missing page.

Do not import `lib/admin.server.ts` from a client component. The account menu learns about access through `AdminAccess`, a boolean passed from the server. The email list stays on the server.

The page reads counts from `profile`, `wait_alert`, `push_subscription`, and `schedule`, plus the camera rows and the cached CBP snapshot. It also reads one row set per table (`profile`, `streak`, `preference`, `wait_alert`, `schedule`, `push_subscription`, plus `usage_event` via `readUsageTotals()`) and joins them in memory by account id in `buildInsights()` (`lib/admin-insights.ts`, client-safe, tested in `tests/admin-insights.test.ts`). A missing table counts as empty. That one model feeds every section: the Journey funnel (signed in, said how they found us, came back, saved a crossing, set an alert or alarm, turned on notifications, asked), Growth (new accounts per day), Where they came from (each source with how many came back and set up crossings), Accounts (searchable, filterable, expandable `AccountList` with every fact for the person and links between inviter and invitees), Crossings (people who saved, alerted, or scheduled each port beside its current wait), and Invites. Accounts are capped at `ACCOUNT_LIMIT`. The page does not write those tables, except `ensureProfile` for the admin on that visit. It does not show push endpoints.
